    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1821">

                <pb facs="1465" n="1349" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg1349"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 367.11/39A.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the American
                        Ambassador</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-11-11">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 11, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Treasury Department is holding at Port Said, subject to your Embassy’s
                    recommendations, the revenue cutter <hi rendition="#italic">Unalga</hi>, to
                    whose <pb facs="1466" n="1350" xml:id="pg1350"/> commander you will telegraph
                    directly your decision in view of situation in Turkey.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
